{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ReactorRouter"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"§22.10’s handler is ONE function from an event to one answer, which is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"right shape for the wire and the wrong shape for the code. A reactor","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"registered for three events opens with a ","type":"text"},{"code":"switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"code":"event.event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and that","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"switch is where two defects live. The first is cheap: a misspelled event name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binds nothing and is discovered as an event that never fires. The second is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not — it is the "},{"code":"default:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" arm that returns "},{"code":".allow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on behalf of code that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never ran, which is §22.10 rule 2’s defect relocated into user code where the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rule does not reach it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A BUILDER RATHER THAN AN ATTRIBUTE"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and §22.14 records why: a Swift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reactor handler is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"type":"text","text":" closure, and collecting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"type":"text","text":" members by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reflection costs a runtime dependency an SDK should not add to hand out an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute. A builder type-checks the closure against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(ReactorEvent) async throws -> ReactorAnswer"},{"type":"text","text":" at compile time, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stricter than what the reflection would have bought. Kotlin made the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trade for the same reason."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PURE SUGAR."}]},{"type":"text","text":" It opens no connection, consumes no queue, verifies no event,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signs no reply and interprets no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timeout_ms"},{"type":"text","text":"; its output is exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handler the runtime accepts (rule 1)."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/reactorrouter"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Bind one handler per event and let the SDK compose them into the single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/reactorServe(config:transport:handler:)"},{"text":" takes.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/init()"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/A